>> title: Crème Anglaise
>> category: Custards & Puddings
>> tags: custard, cream, vanilla, sauce, stovetop
>> servings: 8
>> time: 30 min
>> step.4: cook to 180°F (82°C)
>> step.5: strain, then chill over ice

Heat @whole milk{1%cup}(240 mL), @heavy cream{1%cup}(240 mL), @vanilla bean{1%whole}(split, seeds scraped in), @table salt{1/8%tsp} in a #saucepan{} until steaming.

Whisk @egg yolks{6%large}(110 g), @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}(100 g) to a pale ribbon.

Temper @&(~1)yolks{} with @&(~2)hot milk{}.

Cook @&(~1)custard{} over medium-low, stirring constantly, until it coats a spoon at 180°F (82°C).

Strain @&(~1)sauce{} into a bowl set in ice water and stir until cold.
